Attribution & Upstream Project:
This package is a composable React implementation developed from the architectural
foundation of the original vanilla JavaScript accessibility plugin maintained at:
https://github.com/prabothcharith/accessibility-plugin

Third-Party Assets & Licensure:
- Zero Runtime Dependencies: This library has no runtime dependencies outside of
  peer dependencies on React and React DOM.
- Fonts: No third-party binary font files (.woff, .woff2, .ttf) are bundled. All font
  presets utilize client-system font stacks (e.g. system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif)
  with fallback declarations.
- Icons: All decorative icons are authored directly as inline SVG elements under the
  package's ISC License.
- Dictionaries: Built-in glossaries (English, Sinhala, Tamil) are compiled in-tree
  under the ISC License for client-side offline dictionary lookup with zero external
  network dependencies.
- Speech & Audio: Voice navigation and text-to-speech read-aloud functionality utilize
  native browser platform APIs (window.speechSynthesis, window.SpeechRecognition)
  with zero remote speech services or binary audio assets.
